      "text": "Welcome to Manila, GumberBear international Fans! ðµð­â¨\n\nIf youâre flying in for the LenaMiu Fan Meet at UP Theater, hereâs a quick guide to help you get there safely and smoothly:\n\nâï¸ From Ninoy Aquino International Airport (NAIA):\n\nThe most convenient option is booking a ride via Grab. Itâs safer, fixed-rate, and easier, especially if itâs your first time in Manila. Just input âUP Theaterâ as your destination.\n\nð Travel time: around 1 to 1.5 hours depending on traffic (Manila traffic is real ð\u0085).\n\nð Public transport:\nItâs cheaper, but can be confusing (multiple transfers like jeepneys, MRT, buses). If youâre not familiar with the system, Grab is highly recommended.\n\nâ ï¸ Friendly reminders:\nâ¢ Stay vigilant with your belongings at all times\nâ¢ Avoid unofficial taxis or random offers outside the airport\nâ¢ Some may overcharge foreigners, always check prices first\nâ¢ Keep your phone charged for navigation & booking rides\n\nIf your hotel is already around Quezon City / near UP Theater, just book a ðð«ðð ride for the easiest and safest trip to the venue. Itâs convenient, fixed-price, and less hassle, especially for international fans. ð\n\nð From nearby hotels, travel time is usually around 10â20 minutes depending on traffic.\n\nStay safe, plan ahead, and see you all at UP Theater! ðµð­â¨\n\n#LenaMiu #à¸¥à¸µà¸à¹à¸²à¸«à¸¡à¸´à¸§\n#MiuNatsha #à¸«à¸¡à¸´à¸§à¸à¸±à¸à¸à¸²\n#lalinalena #à¸¥à¸µà¸à¹à¸²à¸¥à¸¥à¸´à¸à¸²",
